The pre-startup safety review shall confirm that prior to the introduction of highly hazardous chemicals to a process:
(i) construction and equipment is in accordance with design specifications;
(ii) safety, operating, maintenance, and emergency procedures are in place and are adequate;
(iii) for new facilities, a process hazard analysis has been performed and recommendations have been resolved or implemented before startup; for modified facilities, the requirement in §1910.119(l) (management of change) has been met;
(iv) training of each employee involved in operating the process has been completed.
